<title>UK: Courtaulds down, SBC Warburg cuts to &quot;hold&quot;.</title>
<headline>Courtaulds down, SBC Warburg cuts to &quot;hold&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in chemical group Courtaulds Plc dropped on Tuesday as analysts at SBC Warburg cut their rating on the stock to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy,&quot; market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 4p at 477 by 0839 GMT, after yesterday closing at its highest level since June 1995.</p>
<p>Traders said the downgrade came after Courtaulds reached Warburg's price target. Analysts at the brokerage were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
